              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "लारै (lārai) is a tadbhava, a word inherited and reshaped by sound change. It comes from lārā, \"string, line\", a form CDIAL reconstructs from its descendants. CDIAL lists Old Marwari lāra under it (CDIAL 11024). The Old Marwari row means \"at the back, behind\"; Gujarati has lāre, \"behind\"."
